        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles Laughton, Fredric March, Frances Drake, Elsa Lanchester, Victor Hugo\n- Works: Les Misérables, Les Misérables (1935 film)\n- Topics: Film adaptation, Marriage, Acting careers\n\nFacts:\n- In 1927, Charles Laughton was cast in a play with his future wife Elsa Lanchester, and they lived and worked together until his death.\n- Charles Laughton and Elsa Lanchester had no children.\n- Les Misérables is a 1935 American drama film based on Victor Hugo's novel Les Misérables.\n- Les Misérables stars Fredric March and Charles Laughton.\n- Frances Drake was born on October 22, 1912.\n- In 1935, Frances Drake played Eponine in Les Misérables.\n- Frances Drake was an American actress best known for playing Eponine in Les Misérables.\n- Frances Drake died on January 18, 2000.",
